dimensions_checked.result:
Found:
- the refusal text is cut by the status line's ellipsis (m1);
- the settings-in-force step flips to Exact on a (1,1) PC (m7).

Checked and fine:
- volume roots and UNC share roots (IsRoot);
- H+S junctions such as 'Documents and Settings' (their own attributes are read, and the refusal is correct);
- desktop.ini;
- deny-all folders (attributes are read through the parent's list right, U-107);
- the pagefile.sys sharing violation (.NET's File.GetAttributes falls back to FindFirstFile);
- a vanished hidden item (NoLongerExists keeps precedence).

Found: the 'injected view asserts refusals only' rule is held by memory. The seam could enforce it by intersecting with the real view (m2).

The other invariants hold by construction:
- refusal never calls open, and the delegate is called only for Hidden, non-root targets (both in Walk);
- the naming predicate lives in Core (HiddenBy);
- the P/Invoke is confined to ShellReveal.cs by rule.

One residual: RevealOutcome still exposes Hidden, System and View, so a later App edit could re-derive the predicate. No rule stops that (low risk; not filed).

Found: a failure to arm the override (member or type not found) is unspecified. It must end the app before Main, as ArmFailListing does, or reveals run under the real view and open windows unattended (m3).

Checked and fine:
- the attribute read failing (fail-open, kept from SL-088);
- the pidl freed on the refusal path (the return is inside the try);
- an open failure after a visible verdict (unchanged).

Strong Core coverage:
- an attribute × view theory on real %TEMP% items;
- precedence Facts;
- decode Facts;
- a real-call Fact against the registry;
- a volume-root Fact;
- real SVI and pagefile.sys reads.

All three App text branches are reached through R-003 (two by injection, one at the real settings).

Gaps:
- the real-system Fact hard-codes C:\pagefile.sys (m8);
- no case or mutant covers the hook refusing an unarmable override (folded into m3);
- the decode Fact cannot catch a bit-15 runtime surprise, because ShowSuperHidden=1 has never been seen (filed for a person by the design).
